{"chunk_id": "c-ad40d374beee67d9", "claim_id": "A027-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/commands/operator/init", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A027", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "During initialization, Vault generates a root key, which is stored in the storage backend alongside all other Vault data. The root key itself is encrypted and requires an _unseal key_ to decrypt it.\n\nThe default Vault configuration uses [Shamir's Secret Sharing](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shamir%", "span_end": 790, "span_start": 372, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-ad40d374beee67d9", "claim_id": "A027-c2", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/commands/operator/init", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A027", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "A certain threshold of shards is required to reconstruct the root key, which is then used to decrypt the Vault's encryption key.", "span_end": 919, "span_start": 791, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-f7ebe6e72a67cb30", "claim_id": "A027-c3", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/concepts/seal", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A027", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "When you start a Vault server, it starts in a sealed state. In this state, Vault can access the physical storage, but it cannot decrypt any of the data on it.", "span_end": 173, "span_start": 15, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-666c2adda4fbaf18", "claim_id": "A028-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/concepts/seal", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A028", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Just as the Shamir seal initialization process yields unseal keys, initializing operations with auto unseal yields recovery keys.", "span_end": 1150, "span_start": 1021, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-666c2adda4fbaf18", "claim_id": "A028-c2", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/concepts/seal", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A028", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "There are certain Vault operations besides unsealing that require a quorum of users to perform, for example, generating a root token. When you use a Shamir seal, you must provide the unseal keys to authorize these operations. When you use auto unseal, these operations require recovery keys instead.", "span_end": 1019, "span_start": 720, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-5af375d1e85dbbcc", "claim_id": "A028-c3", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "api-docs/system/init", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A028", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Please be reminded that recovery keys are used as an authentication flow for rekeying and regeneration of root credentials and cannot be used to unseal Vault in the case of the unavailability of the seal mechanism.", "span_end": 3201, "span_start": 2985, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-b8df6f785eff03af", "claim_id": "A029-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/concepts/tokens", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A029", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Root tokens are tokens that have the `root` policy attached to them. Root tokens can do anything in Vault. _Anything_.", "span_end": 225, "span_start": 107, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-b8df6f785eff03af", "claim_id": "A029-c2", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/concepts/tokens", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A029", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "In addition, they are the only type of token within Vault that can be set to never expire without any renewal needed.", "span_end": 343, "span_start": 226, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-c4c3618bd19c4589", "claim_id": "A029-c3", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/concepts/policies", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A029", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "There is no way to modify the policies associated with a token once the token has been issued. The token must be revoked and a new one acquired to receive a new set of policies.", "span_end": 5494, "span_start": 5317, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-174759581c000682", "claim_id": "A030-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/secrets", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A030", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Other secrets engines connect to other services and generate dynamic credentials on demand.", "span_end": 479, "span_start": 388, "supported": true}
