{"chunk_id": "c-174759581c000682", "claim_id": "A030-c3", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/secrets", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A030", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "since secret leases are tied to the path where they were created.", "span_end": 2044, "span_start": 1977, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-183fb540c58b91b6", "claim_id": "A032-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/concepts/identity", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A032", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Vault Identity can tie authentications from various auth methods to a single representation. This representation of a consolidated identity is called an **Entity** and their corresponding accounts with authentication providers can be mapped as **Aliases**.", "span_end": 905, "span_start": 649, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-6e7deb63f76cd66e", "claim_id": "A032-c2", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/concepts/client-count", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A032", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "**Entity aliases** let clients authenticate with multiple methods but still be associated with a single policy, share resources, and count as the same entity, regardless of the authentication method used for a particular session.", "span_end": 1783, "span_start": 1554, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-4c6b1a36a405eff8", "claim_id": "A032-c3", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/concepts/client-count/faq", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A032", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Clients are only counted once within a billing period, regardless of how many times that client is active and when that client authenticates to a cluster, it has unlimited access to that cluster for the remainder of the billing period.", "span_end": 2754, "span_start": 2519, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-607a4bf2dd9478b3", "claim_id": "A033-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/audit", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A033", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "By default, Vault only writes a keyed hash (HMAC-SHA256) of most string values to audit logs to protect the confidentiality of potentially sensitive information.", "span_end": 529, "span_start": 368, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-a0adfbc680b1099e", "claim_id": "A033-c2", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/audit", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A033", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "As a result, if you have audit devices enabled and Vault cannot log information to at least one of the enabled devices, Vault refuses to service the corresponding API request.", "span_end": 3356, "span_start": 3181, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-a0adfbc680b1099e", "claim_id": "A033-c3", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/audit", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A033", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "When all enabled audit devices become unavailable, Vault in effect becomes unavailable as well.", "span_end": 3453, "span_start": 3358, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-f7ebe6e72a67cb30", "claim_id": "A034-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/concepts/seal", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A034", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "When you use the Shamir seal with multiple nodes, you must unseal each node with the required threshold of shares. Vault does not distribute partially unsealed nodes across the cluster.", "span_end": 2213, "span_start": 2028, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-26212d3706d4a4a2", "claim_id": "A036-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/commands/operator/seal", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A036", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "The `operator seal` seals the Vault server. Sealing tells the Vault server to stop responding to any operations until it is unsealed.", "span_end": 150, "span_start": 17, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-26212d3706d4a4a2", "claim_id": "A036-c2", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/commands/operator/seal", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A036", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "When sealed, the Vault server discards its in-memory root key to unlock the data, so it is physically blocked from responding to operations unsealed.", "span_end": 300, "span_start": 151, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-26212d3706d4a4a2", "claim_id": "A036-c3", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/commands/operator/seal", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A036", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "If an unseal is in progress, sealing the Vault will reset the unsealing process.", "span_end": 382, "span_start": 302, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-b0c512b6155a9b42", "claim_id": "A037-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/configuration/prevent-lease-explosions", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A037", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Unchecked lease explosions create a memory drain on the active node, which can cascade to other nodes and result in denial-of-service issues for the entire cluster.", "span_end": 438, "span_start": 274, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-b3550b8e9e5d0aa2", "claim_id": "A037-c2", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/internals/limits", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A037", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Although no technical maximum exists, high lease counts can cause degradation in system performance. We recommend short default time-to-live values on tokens and leases to avoid a large backlog of unexpired leases, or a large number of simultaneous expirations.", "span_end": 745, "span_start": 484, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-1ce122e0a4677993", "claim_id": "A037-c3", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/internals/telemetry/key-metrics", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A037", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "However, if there is a sudden surge in load and numerous leases are generated with this long default TTL, the storage backend can quickly reach its maximum capacity and crash, resulting in unavailability.", "span_end": 270, "span_start": 66, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-80a8d088d0af149b", "claim_id": "A038-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/internals/rotation", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A038", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Vault stores different encryption keys for different purposes.", "span_end": 78, "span_start": 16, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-947a97ed02c3f755", "claim_id": "A038-c2", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/concepts/transform", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A038", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Vault transform creates a new key for each tokenization transformation, which\nhelps ensure a strong cryptographic distinction between different tokenization\nuse cases.", "span_end": 349, "span_start": 182, "supported": true}
